 "comment": "The values of a language that the format refuses or takes (RQ-008, RQ-009, RQ-012), and the classes of php_value, which no PHP writes: one group per member of packages/rust/interface.json in the case convention of binding (G-5). A value of php_value is {\"kind\", \"value\"}: bytes are {\"hex\"}, a map and an object are [key, value] pairs, a key is a text, {\"int\"} or {\"hex\"}, and a reference is {\"id\", \"value\"}, and a list nested deeper than a JSON reader takes is {\"kind\": \"list\", \"repeat\": n, \"value\"}: n lists, each the one item of the one around it, the innermost holding the value (RQ-006). A failure is raises: its kind and category (RQ-010). A value that the format takes is also what to_host gives back for it (RQ-013, U-1). The group php_value holds the cases of the value itself, which the interface contract does not link yet: a value that from_host refuses and the kind of the refusal. {\"host\": <sort>} is a value of a language that is no value of PHP (callable, date, object), and an integer outside the safe integers of JavaScript is its decimal text.",
